{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that repairs GNU C++ code so that it correctly solves the given programming problem. The code reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Repair the following GNU C++ code so that it correctly solves the programming problem. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your repaired code should implement the problem correctly, meaning that it should produce the correct output for any valid input.\nPrint your repaired code and also the confidence score you give to your repair. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<repaired_code>\n<your_repaired_code>\n</repaired_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the problem description:\n<problem_description>\nAs behooves any intelligent schoolboy, Kevin Sun is studying psycowlogy, cowculus, and cryptcowgraphy at the Bovinia State University (BGU) under Farmer Ivan. During his Mathematics of Olympiads (MoO) class, Kevin was confronted with a weird functional equation and needs your help. For two fixed integers k and p, where p is an odd prime number, the functional equation states that  for some function . (This equation should hold for any integer x in the range 0 to p\u2009-\u20091, inclusive.)It turns out that f can actually be many different functions. Instead of finding a solution, Kevin wants you to count the number of distinct functions f that satisfy this equation. Since the answer may be very large, you should print your result modulo 109\u2009+\u20097.\n</problem_description>\n\nHere is the GNU C++ code you have to repair:\n<original_code>\n#include <bits/stdc++.h>\nusing namespace std;\n\nusing i64 = long long;\nusing u64 = unsigned long long;\nusing f80 = long double;\nusing pii = pair<int, int>;\nusing vi = vector<int>;\nusing vii = vector<pii>;\nusing pll = pair<i64, i64>;\n\nconst int MOD = 1000000007;\nconst int INF = 1000000000;\nconst i64 LINF = 1000000000000000000LL;\nconst f80 PI = 2 * acos(0.0);\nconst int MAX_M = 50;\nconst int MAX_N = 1000007;\n\ni64 mod_pow(i64 b, i64 e, i64 m) {\n    i64 r = 1;\n    b %= m;\n    while (e) {\n        if (e & 1) r = (r * b) % m;\n        b = (b * b) % m;\n        e >>= 1;\n    }\n    return r;\n}\n\ni64 recursive_pow(i64 b, i64 e, i64 m) {\n    if (e == 0) return 1 % m;\n    if (e & 1) return (b * recursive_pow(b, e - 1, m)) % m;\n    i64 t = recursive_pow(b, e >> 1, m);\n    return (t * t) % m;\n}\n\nint n, k;\nint mapping[MAX_N];\nbool visited[MAX_N];\n\nvoid execute() {\n    cin >> n >> k;\n    \n    if (k == 0) {\n        cout << mod_pow(k, k - 1);\n        return;\n    }\n    if (k == 1) {\n        cout << mod_pow(k, k);\n        return;\n    }\n    \n    for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {\n        mapping[i] = (i64)i * k % n;\n    }\n    \n    i64 total = 1;\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {\n        if (!visited[i]) {\n            visited[i] = true;\n            int cur = mapping[i];\n            int cycle_size = 1;\n            while (!visited[cur]) {\n                visited[cur] = true;\n                cur = mapping[cur];\n                ++cycle_size;\n            }\n            if (recursive_pow(k, cycle_size, n) == 1) {\n                total = (total * n) % MOD;\n            }\n        }\n    }\n    cout << total;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    ios_base::sync_with_stdio(false);\n    cin.tie(nullptr);\n    \n#ifndef ONLINE_JUDGE\n    freopen(\"in.txt\", \"r\", stdin);\n#endif\n\n    execute();\n    \n#ifdef _LOCAL_\n    // cerr << \"Runtime: \" << (double)clock() / CLOCKS_PER_SEC << \"s\\n\";\n#endif\n    return 0;\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<repaired_code>\n#include <bits/stdc++.h>\nusing namespace std;\n\nusing i64 = long long;\nusing pii = pair<int, int>;\nusing vi = vector<int>;\n\nconst int MOD = 1000000007;\n\ni64 mod_pow(i64 b, i64 e, i64 m) {\n    i64 r = 1;\n    b %= m;\n    while (e) {\n        if (e & 1) r = (r * b) % m;\n        b = (b * b) % m;\n        e >>= 1;\n    }\n    return r;\n}\n\nint n, k;\n\nvoid execute() {\n    cin >> n >> k;\n    \n    // The functional equation is f(k*x mod p) = f(x)\n    // We need to count the number of functions f: {0,1,...,p-1} -> {0,1,...,p-1}\n    // that satisfy f(k*x mod p) = f(x) for all x\n    \n    // The number of such functions is n^(number of cycles in the mapping x -> k*x mod n)\n    // But we need to be careful: the mapping x -> k*x mod n may not be a permutation\n    // if gcd(k, n) != 1. However, the problem states that p is an odd prime.\n    // So n should be p (the prime), and k is fixed.\n    \n    // Actually, re-reading the problem: p is an odd prime, and the domain is 0 to p-1.\n    // So n in the input is actually p.\n    \n    // The functional equation is f(k*x mod p) = f(x)\n    // For x = 0: f(0) = f(0) always true, so 0 forms a fixed point.\n    // For x != 0: since p is prime, the multiplicative group is cyclic of order p-1.\n    // The mapping x -> k*x mod p for x != 0 is a permutation on the nonzero elements\n    // if gcd(k, p) = 1. If k \u2261 0 (mod p), then f(0) = f(x) for all x, so all values must be equal.\n    \n    if (k % n == 0) {\n        // k \u2261 0 (mod n), so f(0) = f(x) for all x, meaning all function values must be equal\n        cout << n;\n        return;\n    }\n    \n    // Count cycles in the mapping x -> (k*x) % n for x in [0, n-1]\n    vi visited(n, 0);\n    i64 total = 1;\n    \n    for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {\n        if (visited[i]) continue;\n        \n        int cur = i;\n        int cycle_len = 0;\n        while (!visited[cur]) {\n            visited[cur] = 1;\n            cycle_len++;\n            cur = (1LL * k * cur) % n;\n        }\n        \n        // For each cycle, we can assign any value from 0 to n-1 independently\n        total = (total * n) % MOD;\n    }\n    \n    cout << total;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    ios_base::sync_with_stdio(false);\n    cin.tie(nullptr);\n    \n    execute();\n    \n    return 0;\n}\n</repaired_code>\n<confidence>\n0.8\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-1.311301275563892e-06, -0.00018416139937471598, -1.9073468138230965e-06, -1.4305104514278355e-06, -0.00010168035078095272, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -1.7165990357170813e-05, -2.1576648578047752e-05, -2.145764938177308e-06, -2.264974000354414e-06, -2.145764938177308e-06, -3.516612196108326e-05, -1.0728830375228426e-06, -1.311301275563892e-06, -1.1920922133867862e-06, -0.0034004980698227882, -0.0010962436208501458, 0.0, -1.2278481335670222e-05, 0.0, -2.0265558760002023e-06, -4.768370445162873e-07, -0.038041986525058746, -0.005950947757810354, -0.5761765241622925, 0.0, -1.3232143828645349e-05, -1.5497195136049413e-06, -2.145764938177308e-06, -2.634490556374658e-05, -0.16023202240467072, -3.421248038648628e-05, -1.4185804502631072e-05, -3.4570634852570947e-06, -1.311301275563892e-06, -9.65590606938349e-06, -0.0485939159989357, -4.291525328881107e-06, -0.0007148809381760657, -5.364403477869928e-06, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0, -4.768360213347478e-06, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0, -1.156323378381785e-05, -6.9141146923357155e-06, -1.1920922133867862e-06, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -0.007607181556522846, -0.0025843337643891573, 0.0, 0.0, -2.098061486321967e-05, -0.00015090756642166525, -1.311301275563892e-06, 0.0, -4.768370445162873e-07, -2.4318398573086597e-05, 0.0, -1.7881377516459906e-06, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -4.887569048150908e-06, -3.576278118089249e-07, -2.3841855067985307e-07, 0.0, 0.0, -2.264974000354414e-06, 0.0, -3.4570634852570947e-06, -4.768370445162873e-07, 0.0, -0.0004555141495075077, 0.0, -7.152555099310121e-07, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0, -1.2993727978027891e-05, 0.0, 0.0, -4.768370445162873e-07, 0.0, -1.311301275563892e-06, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -2.634490556374658e-05, -9.536738616588991e-07, 0.0, -0.00020346